# SEARCH — what does search return for a word or a chip?
# All requests are READ ONLY. See README.md for environments and labels.
#
# Set @searchText for typed searches and @concept for chip searches. Get the
# chip concepts from the first request (main[].concept); each deployment
# can configure them differently.
#
# Reading the response:
#   topPick + results   count both; limit counts only results.
#   resultPath          browse, lexical-only, hybrid, fallback-lexical, semantic-only.
#                       semantic-only is valid even though OpenAPI omits it.
#   nextCursor          more results exist; an empty first page proves nothing.
# Errors: 400 bad JSON or limit outside 1..50 · 409 start over without
# continuationToken · 503 recovery busy, respect Retry-After.
#
# Next page: copy a request and add "continuationToken": "<nextCursor>".
# Embedding problems → 12-embeddings.rest. Reindex a recipe → 07-workflow.rest B1.

@searchText = poultry
@concept = poultry

### READ ONLY — Chip vocabulary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/search/filters
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
X-Family-Member-Id: {{familyMemberId}}

### READ ONLY — Browse (no text, no chip)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
X-Family-Member-Id: {{familyMemberId}}

{
  "query": "",
  "limit": 12,
  "filters": {},
  "preferences": {}
}

### READ ONLY — Typed search (@searchText)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
X-Family-Member-Id: {{familyMemberId}}

{
  "query": "{{searchText}}",
  "limit": 12,
  "filters": {},
  "preferences": {}
}

### READ ONLY — Chip search (@concept, no text)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
X-Family-Member-Id: {{familyMemberId}}

{
  "query": "",
  "limit": 12,
  "filters": {},
  "preferences": {
    "concepts": ["{{concept}}"]
  }
}

### READ ONLY — Chip search limited to Supper
# filters are hard filters and can hide matches; compare with the request above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
X-Family-Member-Id: {{familyMemberId}}

{
  "query": "",
  "limit": 12,
  "filters": {
    "mealTypes": ["Supper"]
  },
  "preferences": {
    "concepts": ["{{concept}}"]
  }
}
